  "worked_solution": "Since we need to divide by $3$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/fe13a38598359a92be567c1a4c3b1e0fb1c4d8c3ed6522dda37171c1ff5f2668.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{2}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}÷3=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$",
